* Why is error an interface?

#lang go

    type NotFoundError struct {
        Path string
    }

    func (e *NotFoundError) Error() string {
        return "not found: " + e.Path
    }

- Every error type can carry its own data (file path, HTTP status, ...)
- The caller still handles every error the same way: *if* *err* *!=* *nil*
- If the details are needed: *errors.As* finds the concrete type

